WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.839
My name is Alfonso Aguirre Rodriguez also known as Mithy and I play support for G2 Esports.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:23.000
I knew I could be good at whatever game I played so

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:29.730
I just wanted to become pro at the next upcoming esport
and I think I started like officially

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:36.329
started probably back towards the
end of season two. Took me like,

00:00:36.329 --> 00:00:42.210
season 3 this when I became a pro. Look at that, Lemondogs forced to run here

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:46.350
as they lose Dexter, Araneae gets popped in the air. Mithy manages to pick up that kill.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:51.180
Lemondogs was a turning
point for me because I was actually now

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:56.280
playing against all the people that I
idolized for a whole year and it was fun

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.899
I learned a lot. I was really like pressuring myself to be good

00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:05.010
and always perform well. I got the Worlds
and I realized, I actually,

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:09.060
the first time I like smashed into a wall and was like fuck I'm bad you know and that

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:13.409
was kind of like what I was looking for
and searching for when I smashed into

00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:17.880
that wall at Worlds I really got a lot
of motivation and I was like oh my god

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.880
like I can be so much better.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:25.230
 

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:29.250
 

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:34.720
I had my time out for toxicity and
everything, but during all that time I

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:39.880
was actually like improving myself as a
player and I think I learned a lot even

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:44.470
though I was in challenger scene and I
got a lot out of it so I knew,

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:48.370
especially on my time out I also had
time to think and I think I coached a group for

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:49.810
like two weeks or something.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:55.750
It wasn't until I joined Origen where I,
finally I would say match the players

00:01:55.750 --> 00:02:01.420
that were not really egoed or biased or like, narrow-minded and actually just

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.750
made me open my mind to different ways
of looking at the game especially

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:08.500
Amazing, he would always like say
something that I wouldn't really

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:13.030
understand. After I looked back at it for a
few times and looked at it closely, it made

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:17.200
sense to me and would make me improve as a player.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:22.870
Origen will place first in Group D after taking down KT Rolster. And with the crowd behind them, Origen go undefeated.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.720
Everyone had their way of talking to
everyone else. Everyone had their own

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:38.750
personalities. Everyone had like, their
small roles within the team and

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:43.430
no one really tried to do more than
their roles because everyone was like

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:47.060
stuck in the same way of viewing the
game and the same way of playing it.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:50.240
I felt that even if I joined a challenger
team I would improve more as a player

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:51.500
than if I stayed in OG.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:55.220
We just didn't have the, probably
coaching staff I can blame it on

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:59.210
that kinda like help us like view things
differently and talk to each other in a

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:03.830
different way and just open our minds to
different situations.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:11.560
I had to make a decision. It was not easy and I stated some of the reasons why I made that decision

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:14.840
in like a public Facebook post. Before I
made the decision I already accepted

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.840
what the consequences of that decision
would be.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:32.920
Apart from the whole winning swap, it
was the only thing that really could

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:39.230
take us both and was willing to like
invest on taking us both so that's kind

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:42.740
of how it went. I wanted to play with
Zven, Zven wanted to play with me and

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:47.810
there was never really a downhill slope
with him so I didn't really see why I

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:53.120
wouldn't keep playing with him if I would
just like be constantly learning like I

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.110
had been for a whole year and a half
before that. I thought it was a safe bet

00:03:57.110 --> 00:04:00.470
to join G2 because four out five
players were already going to click for

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:05.870
sure and then there was Kikis and
Expect. I would say that our

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:09.860
challenge for this split was getting us four to connect with Expect and with Kikis.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:14.510
 

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:17.440
Will it be enough, yes it will.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:23.080
Trashy, another lamb to the
slaughter. Stand united is gonna finish

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:28.420
the channel. Mithy saves everyone!

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:34.120
To say now oh my god things are really going good, we're first and things are great

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:38.260
everyone is working hard, we don't have
issues. But there's going to be a time

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:42.460
where we're going to have issues because
that's just how it works and it's about

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:48.250
how we confront those issues and
work towards them and stay as

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:52.540
a group and just understand them. Things
can go wrong at some point but right

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:56.200
now things are going great so I'm in a
very happy situation.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:13.580
Welcome to the G2 era! They are your summer split champions.

00:05:15.249 --> 00:05:21.099
It was just a dream come true. It
wasn't really something I expected.

00:05:21.099 --> 00:05:24.759
This year I'd say a realistic goal would be to try to make it out of groups, but I

00:05:24.759 --> 00:05:29.679
think that if we take this whole going
to Worlds thing and treat it as

00:05:29.679 --> 00:05:33.219
an experience and just make our
goal like maybe making out of groups

00:05:33.219 --> 00:05:37.449
maybe not, just like with OG but really
like trying to learn as much as we can

00:05:37.449 --> 00:05:42.339
from this experience. I think we can
really put up a very very good performance.

